NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Parallel\" queries are queries that are executed in parallel, or at the same time so as to maximize fetching concurrency."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-parallel-queries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Parallel Queries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the number of parallel queries does not change, there is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no extra effort"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to use parallel queries. Just use any number of TanStack Query's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useInfiniteQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" hooks side-by-side!"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n// The following queries will execute in parallel\nconst usersQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['users'], queryFn: fetchUsers })\nconst teamsQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['teams'], queryFn: fetchTeams })\nconst projectsQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: fetchProjects,\n})\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"dynamic-parallel-queries-with-usequeries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Parallel Queries with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the number of queries you need to execute is changing from render to render, you cannot use manual querying since that would violate the rules of hooks. Instead, TanStack Query provides a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" hook, which you can use to dynamically execute as many queries in parallel as you'd like."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options object"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queries key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" whose value is an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array of query objects"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It returns an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array of query results"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const users = computed(...)\nconst queries = computed(() => users.value.map(user => {\n    return {\n      queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n      queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n    }\n  })\n);\nconst userQueries = useQueries({queries: queries})","lang":"js"}],"headings":[{"id":"manual-parallel-queries","text":"Manual Parallel Queries","level":2},{"id":"dynamic-parallel-queries-with-usequeries","text":"Dynamic Parallel Queries with useQueries","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n\"Parallel\" queries are queries that are executed in parallel, or at the same time so as to maximize fetching concurrency.\n\n## Manual Parallel Queries\n\nWhen the number of parallel queries does not change, there is **no extra effort** to use parallel queries. Just use any number of TanStack Query's `useQuery` and `useInfiniteQuery` hooks side-by-side!\n\n\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n// The following queries will execute in parallel\nconst usersQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['users'], queryFn: fetchUsers })\nconst teamsQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['teams'], queryFn: fetchTeams })\nconst projectsQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: fetchProjects,\n})\n</script>\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n## Dynamic Parallel Queries with `useQueries`\n\nIf the number of queries you need to execute is changing from render to render, you cannot use manual querying since that would violate the rules of hooks. Instead, TanStack Query provides a `useQueries` hook, which you can use to dynamically execute as many queries in parallel as you'd like.\n\n`useQueries` accepts an **options object** with a **queries key** whose value is an **array of query objects**. It returns an **array of query results**:\n\n\n\n```js\nconst users = computed(...)\nconst queries = computed(() => users.value.map(user => {\n    return {\n      queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n      queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n    }\n  })\n);\nconst userQueries = useQueries({queries: queries})\n```\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: parallel-queries\ntitle: Parallel Queries\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/parallel-queries.md\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\n// The following queries will execute in parallel\nconst usersQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['users'], queryFn: fetchUsers })\nconst teamsQuery = useQuery({ queryKey: ['teams'], queryFn: fetchTeams })\nconst projectsQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  queryFn: fetchProjects,\n})\n</script>\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n[//]: # 'Info'\n[//]: # 'Info'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```js\nconst users = computed(...)\nconst queries = computed(() => users.value.map(user => {\n    return {\n      queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n      queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n    }\n  })\n);\nconst userQueries = useQueries({queries: queries})\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n"}
